[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +After DEC-0001 selects the framework, package manager, and CI baseline, create
[stderr] +the smallest reproducible project skeleton for the shared game core, web
[stderr] +adapter, and PWA adapter. Document one bootstrap, format, lint, and
[stderr] +deterministic test command interface, and make a clean approved-runtime
[stderr] +checkout run a deterministic sample test. This task establishes boundaries and
[stderr] +tooling only; it does not implement game behaviour or resolve the decision.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependencies
[stderr] +
[stderr] +This is the first implementation contract and has no R-series dependencies.
[stderr] +GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 is retained as a human implementation precondition:
[stderr] +authoring this runbook does not select a stack, and implementation must stop
[stderr] +before selecting or installing framework, package-manager, or CI tooling.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Root build and tooling configuration, including the pinned toolchain
[stderr] +  declaration and command mapping.
[stderr] +- `src/core/`, `src/content/`, `src/app/`, `src/platform/web/`, and
[stderr] +  `src/platform/pwa/` ownership directories, created without feature code.
[stderr] +- `tests/` and an isolated deterministic sample-test location.
[stderr] +- `docs/development.md`, which records the approved-runtime bootstrap,
[stderr] +  format, lint, and deterministic-test commands once DEC-0001 is decided.
[stderr] +- The build/test command interface: `bootstrap`, `format`, `lint`, and
[stderr] +  `test:deterministic` (or the selected tool's documented equivalent).
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Use the DEC-0001-approved runtime only. Pin its version and package-manager
[stderr] +lock/metadata as appropriate to that approved selection. Create the isolated
[stderr] +directory skeleton so later work has distinct shared-core, content, app,
[stderr] +web-adapter, PWA-adapter, and test ownership.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Configure the selected tooling so the documented command interface has a
[stderr] +single reproducible mapping for bootstrap, formatting, linting, and a
[stderr] +deterministic sample test. The sample test must use no wall clock, network,
[stderr] +player data, browser storage, renderer, or platform feature. Record the exact
[stderr] +commands and a clean-checkout result in `docs/development.md`.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The skeleton must preserve the canonical direction: target adapters are
[stderr] +separate from the shared deterministic core, and no directory implies that a
[stderr] +target may change campaign rules. Later R0002 owns enforcement of detailed
[stderr] +core/adapter dependency rules.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The responsive web and installable PWA targets receive separate adapter
[stderr] +directories only. Neither adapter gains a renderer, service worker, cache
[stderr] +lifecycle, browser API dependency, or target-specific campaign behaviour in
[stderr] +this task. PWA installation, caching, offline delivery, and update activation
[stderr] +remain later scoped work; the PWA directory is an ownership boundary, not an
[stderr] +implementation of those features.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Non-goals
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Do not resolve DEC-0001 or choose a framework, package manager, CI provider,
[stderr] +host, storage API, browser/device matrix, or performance budget. Do not add
[stderr] +gameplay, campaign state, content, UI screens, renderer code, input handling,
[stderr] +service worker, persistence, network client, accounts, diagnostics, hosting,
[stderr] +or release automation. Do not claim browser/PWA compatibility or release
[stderr] +readiness.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Asset assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. The baseline contains only source,
[stderr] +configuration, test, and developer-documentation boundaries. Do not create or
[stderr] +add incidental product visuals, UI assets, illustrations, icons, fonts,
[stderr] +textures, sprites, maps, audio-visual assets, or copied reference styling;
[stderr] +`asset_ids` remains blank.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Audio assessment
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`. Do not create, add, reserve, or reference
[stderr] +music, sound effects, voice, or other product audio; the blank audio metadata
[stderr] +and zero duration intentionally record that exclusion.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Verification
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Before implementation, confirm DEC-0001 is accepted and record the approved
[stderr] +  runtime, package manager, CI baseline, and pinned versions. If it remains
[stderr] +  unresolved, stop implementation and report GATE-0001 without substituting a
[stderr] +  tool choice.
[stderr] +- In a clean checkout of the approved runtime, run the exact documented
[stderr] +  bootstrap command, format check, lint check, and deterministic sample-test
[stderr] +  command.
[stderr] +- Verify the documented ownership directories exist and that the sample test
[stderr] +  is isolated from browser, network, storage, clock, and product data.
[stderr] +- Preserve command output, pinned-toolchain evidence, directory listing, and
[stderr] +  the deterministic test result in the implementation evidence.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`docs/development.md` must identify the selected command mapping and pinned
[stderr] +toolchain only after DEC-0001. The implementation record must retain the clean
[stderr] +checkout command outputs and show the isolated ownership directories. If the
[stderr] +gate is still blocked, retain this runbook and record that no implementation
[stderr] +tooling or product work was created.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- An approved-runtime clean checkout can run the documented bootstrap, format,
[stderr] +  lint, and deterministic sample-test commands successfully.
[stderr] +- Shared core, content, app, web-adapter, PWA-adapter, and test ownership
[stderr] +  directories are isolated without feature, renderer, storage, or service
[stderr] +  implementation.
[stderr] +- GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 remains explicit; this task neither selects the stack
[stderr] +  nor claims implementation, browser, PWA, or release readiness before that
[stderr] +  decision.
[stderr] +- No product visual or audio asset is created or introduced.
