gated foundation\",\"state\":\"accepted\",\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 is retained inside R0001 and blocks implementation only\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0001\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/platform-appendix.md\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0001\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validated R0001 metadata, provenance, output ownership, explicit GATE-0001 disposition, and baseline-command evidence; batch checkpoint complete\",\"recovery\":\"keep R0001 reserved; author it before, not after, the gate\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"one bounded R runbook\",\"gate is explicit\",\"baseline command and ownership evidence are specified\"]},\n     {\"id\":\"B0002\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"Shared seams, deterministic harness, and token contract\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"R0001 is an implementation dependency only; R0010 retains GATE-0002,GATE-0004\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0010\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0002\",\"IMP-0003\",\"IMP-0010\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate the three contracts and record any gate-blocked subwork\",\"recovery\":\"repair only R0002,R0003,R0010; never split or renumber accepted contracts\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"core/adapter seam precedes feature work\",\"fixture and token outputs have distinct ownership\",\"all gates retained\"]},\n     {\"id\":\"B0003\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"Deterministic state slice and connected-scope exclusion\",\"state\":\"accepted\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0002\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0002 accepted\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0004\",\"R0008\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0004\",\"IMP-0008\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validated R0004/R0008 metadata, provenance, dependencies, ownership, and required sections against the manifest\",\"recovery\":\"retain IDs and repair the failed R contract only\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"vertical foundation slice remains independently reviewable\",\"P0 connected-service exclusion is explicit\"]},\n     {\"id\":\"B0004\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"Content validation and local recovery protocols\",\"state\":\"planned\",\"depends_on_batches\":[\"B0003\"],\"parallel_with\":[],\"preceding_decision\":\"B0003 accepted; R0006 requires GATE-0003\",\"r_contract_ids\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"context_packet\":{\"specification\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#save-recovery-and-offline-persistence\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0005\",\"IMP-0006\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"validate content/save boundaries and retained storage gate\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0005,R0006 and rerun the blocked item after its decision\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"content and save/cache ownership is separated\",\"save recovery remains a bounded foundation slice\"]},\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..96d929a19a547a69d4a3214072eb64346549f2e8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@\n+---\n+task_id: R0001\n+sequence: 1\n+title: Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\n+dependencies: []\n+requirement_ids:\n+  - NFR-0010\n+  - NFR-0012\n+source_specifications:\n+  - specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\n+  - specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\n+source_catalogue_ids:\n+  - IMP-0001\n+authoring_batch: B0001\n+factory_stages:\n+  - F011\n+  - F012\n+  - F013\n+asset_impact: not_applicable\n+asset_ids:\n+asset_brief: No product asset work; establish only project/tooling boundaries and prohibit incidental assets.\n+audio_impact: not_applicable\n+audio_ids:\n+audio_brief:\n+audio_duration_seconds: 0\n+audio_loop: not_applicable\n+audio_style_version:\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+After DEC-0001 selects the framework, package manager, and CI baseline, create\n+the smallest reproducible project skeleton for the shared game core, web\n+adapter, and PWA adapter. Document one bootstrap, format, lint, and\n+deterministic test command interface, and make a clean approved-runtime\n+checkout run a deterministic sample test. This task establishes boundaries and\n+tooling only; it does not implement game behaviour or resolve the decision.\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+This is the first implementation contract and has no R-series dependencies.\n+GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 is retained as a human implementation precondition:\n+authoring this runbook does not select a stack, and implementation must stop\n+before selecting or installing framework, package-manager, or CI tooling.\n+\n+## Ownership\n+\n+- Root build and tooling configuration, including the pinned toolchain\n+  declaration and command mapping.\n+- `src/core/`, `src/content/`, `src/app/`, `src/platform/web/`, and\n+  `src/platform/pwa/` ownership directories, created without feature code.\n+- `tests/` and an isolated deterministic sample-test location.\n+- `docs/development.md`, which records the approved-runtime bootstrap,\n+  format, lint, and deterministic-test commands once DEC-0001 is decided.\n+- The build/test command interface: `bootstrap`, `format`, `lint`, and\n+  `test:deterministic` (or the selected tool's documented equivalent).\n+\n+## Behaviour\n+\n+Use the DEC-0001-approved runtime only. Pin its version and package-manager\n+lock/metadata as appropriate to that approved selection. Create the isolated\n+directory skeleton so later work has distinct shared-core, content, app,\n+web-adapter, PWA-adapter, and test ownership.\n+\n+Configure the selected tooling so the documented command interface has a\n+single reproducible mapping for bootstrap, formatting, linting, and a\n+deterministic sample test. The sample test must use no wall clock, network,\n+player data, browser storage, renderer, or platform feature. Record the exact\n+commands and a clean-checkout result in `docs/development.md`.\n+\n+The skeleton must preserve the canonical direction: target adapters are\n+separate from the shared deterministic core, and no directory implies that a\n+target may change campaign rules. Later R0002 owns enforcement of detailed\n+core/adapter dependency rules.\n+\n+## Web and PWA differences\n+\n+The responsive web and installable PWA targets receive separate adapter\n+directories only. Neither adapter gains a renderer, service worker, cache\n+lifecycle, browser API dependency, or target-specific campaign behaviour in\n+this task. PWA installation, caching, offline delivery, and update activation\n+remain later scoped work; the PWA directory is an ownership boundary, not an\n+implementation of those features.\n+\n+## Non-goals\n+\n+Do not resolve DEC-0001 or choose a framework, package manager, CI provider,\n+host, storage API, browser/device matrix, or performance budget. Do not add\n+gameplay, campaign state, content, UI screens, renderer code, input handling,\n+service worker, persistence, network client, accounts, diagnostics, hosting,\n+or release automation. Do not claim browser/PWA compatibility or release\n+readiness.\n+\n+## Asset assessment\n+\n+`asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. The baseline contains only source,\n+configuration, test, and developer-documentation boundaries. Do not create or\n+add incidental product visuals, UI assets, illustrations, icons, fonts,\n+textures, sprites, maps, audio-visual assets, or copied reference styling;\n+`asset_ids` remains blank.\n+\n+## Audio assessment\n+\n+`audio_impact` is `not_applicable`. Do not create, add, reserve, or reference\n+music, sound effects, voice, or other product audio; the blank audio metadata\n+and zero duration intentionally record that exclusion.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+- Before implementation, confirm DEC-0001 is accepted and record the approved\n+  runtime, package manager, CI baseline, and pinned versions. If it remains\n+  unresolved, stop implementation and report GATE-0001 without substituting a\n+  tool choice.\n+- In a clean checkout of the approved runtime, run the exact documented\n+  bootstrap command, format check, lint check, and deterministic sample-test\n+  command.\n+- Verify the documented ownership directories exist and that the sample test\n+  is isolated from browser, network, storage, clock, and product data.\n+- Preserve command output, pinned-toolchain evidence, directory listing, and\n+  the deterministic test result in the implementation evidence.\n+\n+## Evidence\n+\n+`docs/development.md` must identify the selected command mapping and pinned\n+toolchain only after DEC-0001. The implementation record must retain the clean\n+checkout command outputs and show the isolated ownership directories. If the\n+gate is still blocked, retain this runbook and record that no implementation\n+tooling or product work was created.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- An approved-runtime clean checkout can run the documented bootstrap, format,\n+  lint, and deterministic sample-test commands successfully.\n+- Shared core, content, app, web-adapter, PWA-adapter, and test ownership\n+  directories are isolated without feature, renderer, storage, or service\n+  implementation.\n+- GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 remains explicit; this task neither selects the stack\n+  nor claims implementation, browser, PWA, or release readiness before that\n+  decision.\n+- No product visual or audio asset is created or introduced.\n\ntokens used\n81,625\n", "adapter_log": "", "test_log": "R0001 and B0001 structural validation: PASS\nManifest JSON parse: PASS\ngit diff --check: PASS", "browser_log": "Not applicable; no browser behavior changed.", "screenshots": []}, "acceptance_results": [{"criterion": "Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Created projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md with task_id R0001, source_catalogue_ids IMP-0001, authoring_batch B0001, and no other R-series file."}, {"criterion": "R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Structural validation passed for required front matter, provenance fields, required sections, asset_impact: not_applicable, blank asset IDs, and explicit asset/audio exclusions."}, {"criterion": "Existing conflicting R0001 content causes a stop and report rather than an overwrite.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Focused file discovery found no pre-existing R0001.md before creation; no existing contract was overwritten."}, {"criterion": "Manifest ownership and checkpoint state are updated only after structural validation passes.", "status": "pass", "evidence": "Initial R0001 structural validation passed before updating B0001 to accepted and recording its completed checkpoint; final linkage/checkpoint validation also passed."}], "documentation": {"reviewed_files": ["projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/PROJECT_BRIEF.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/README.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/01-product-brief.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/03-technical-contract.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/specification/platform-appendix.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json", "runbooks/TEMPLATE.md", "runbooks/F014.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0002.md"], "updated_files": ["projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md", "projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json"], "summary": "R0001 is the required developer-facing implementation contract. No README update was needed because no project behavior, setup command, or architecture was implemented."}, "known_limitations": ["GATE-0001 / DEC-0001 remains unresolved by design. R0001 records it as an implementation precondition and does not select tooling or implement the game."], "browser_coverage": "Not applicable: this task authored an implementation runbook and manifest checkpoint only; it changed no browser behavior and requires no Playwright spec.", "recommended_next_step": "complete"}


